  "limitations": [
    "Eleven clusters spanning only R500 = 1054 to 1430 kpc cannot constrain the sharpness m of the crossover; only that galaxies sit at tau = 1 and these clusters near tau = 2.",
    "X-ray hydrostatic masses carry their own known bias of order ten to twenty percent, which is the same size as the residual scatter here.",
    "tau = 2 is a claim that the companion is a free-streaming radial null flux in clusters. That is a physical statement needing its own independent check; this test only shows the number it implies is the number the data wants.",
